Parlance for Ubuntu
===================

  /usr/bin/parlance         the app (window + tray)
  /usr/bin/parlance-model   model CLI: list | use | status | check | download [<model>] [--replace]
  /usr/lib/parlance/        app code + bundled sherpa-onnx (not in Ubuntu)
  ~/.config/parlance/       config.json
  ~/.local/share/parlance/  models/<model>/<version>/, state.json

Pick a model in the Model tab; each is ~660 MB and downloads once. For the hotkey, join the input
group and log in again:  sudo usermod -aG input $USER
The bundled wheels match the python3 minor version the package was built for;
rebuild after Ubuntu moves python3 to a new minor version.
